# LLM configuration for Campaign Studio — story generation and live weeks.
#
# Copy this file to llm.env (same directory, next to TUTORIAL.md) and fill
# in what you use. llm.env is git-ignored: the key stays on your machine
# and goes only to the endpoint below. Any OpenAI-compatible
# /chat/completions endpoint works.
#
# Precedence: environment variables (LLM_BASE_URL / LLM_API_KEY /
# LLM_MODEL) override this file. With everything unset, the studio falls
# back to its built-in Z.ai coding-plan defaults: the coding endpoint plus
# the key from $ZAI_API_KEY (or the key stored by the ZCode CLI in
# ~/.zcode/v2/provider_config.json). The model default is glm-5.3-flash.
#
# NOTE: a custom LLM_BASE_URL requires LLM_MODEL — the model name is
# provider-specific and the studio refuses to guess.

# --- Z.ai coding-plan (built-in default; this block is what llm.env is
#     NOT needed for — shown here for completeness) -----------------------
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.z.ai/api/coding/paas/v4
# LLM_API_KEY=
# LLM_MODEL=glm-5.3-flash

# --- OpenAI -------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=sk-...
# LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# --- OpenRouter ---------------------------------------------------------
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=sk-or-...
# LLM_MODEL=anthropic/claude-3.5-haiku

# --- Ollama (local, free, offline; any key string is fine) --------------
# LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=ollama
# LLM_MODEL=llama3.1
